Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 13:54:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 10/11] tokens: renew the account's session in its last week

A license request exchanges the signed-in account's Passport session,
which sign-in stores under user-tokens and Live issues for ninety days.
Nothing renewed it, so ninety days after a sign-in the license request
could only say "not logged in: ... has expired; sign in again" -- a
sign-in through the same page some systems cannot get past (issue #366)
-- for every install that signed in when the downloader was new.

While Live still takes the session, it issues a new one for it without a
sign-in: asked for http://Passport.NET/tb with this device's session, it
answers with the session itself, keyed http://Passport.NET/STS, for
another ninety days. The license request now does that when the session
it is about to use ends within a week, stores the new one, and carries
on with the old one if Live does not issue it.

Tested against Live on a copy of a keyring whose account session was
set to end in two days: the license was issued, and the copy held a new
session ending ninety days later.
